  "description": "Governed Stripe accounts receivable, eighteen commands under stripe.billing.*. Covers the full cycle: find or create a customer, bill_client chains find-or-create plus draft plus send behind one approval, aging_report buckets every open invoice by days overdue, customer_summary rolls up profile plus invoices plus subscriptions plus lifetime paid in one call, credit_note_create and refund_create close out invoices two different ways depending on whether the money already moved, plus coupons and promotion codes for collections work that needs an incentive. Eight commands run without approval, ten go through the airlock. Every money-moving call carries a Stripe Idempotency-Key derived from the airlock payload hash, so an approved action can never fire twice; a missing idempotency helper is a hard error, not a silent fallback. Auth is a single Stripe secret key held in the local vault, declared in a top-level auth block. Works with sk_test_ keys end to end. contest:2026Q3",
